# Project Structure

- Two-module monorepo: `api/` (FastAPI + LangGraph backend) and `ui/` (Streamlit chat client)
- Managed with **uv** and Python 3.14+
- Configuration via root `.env` loaded by `api/app/settings.py` (Pydantic BaseSettings)
- Docker Compose for local multi-service runs

# Architecture

- Package-by-domain: `agents/`, `workflow/`, `rag/`, `schemas/`, `integrations/`, `guardrails/`
- ABC for swappable implementations (e.g., `MovieFinderAgent` → TMDB or in-memory)
- Factory functions for LLM models, retrievers, and graph nodes
- Module-level singletons initialized in FastAPI `lifespan`, injected into routers
- Structured LLM output via `llm.with_structured_output(PydanticModel)`
- Resilience: every LLM call has a deterministic fallback on failure

# LangGraph Conventions

- Single `StateGraph(MovieNightState)` compiled in `MovieNightWorkflow`
- State is a `TypedDict(total=False)` — fields are added incrementally by nodes
- Nodes are closures returned by `create_*_node(agent)` factory functions
- Routing logic lives in pure functions in `workflow/routing.py`
- Evaluation loop: writer → evaluator → retry (max 3), tracked via `retry_count` and `rejected_titles`
- When adding a new node: create agent class, add factory node function, wire into graph with conditional edges

# Adding New Agents

- Create agent class in `api/app/agents/` with a clear single responsibility
- Define any structured output models in `api/app/schemas/`
- Create a `create_<name>_node()` factory in `workflow/nodes.py`
- Add new state fields (if needed) to `MovieNightState` with `total=False`
- Wire the node into the graph in `workflow/graph.py` with routing in `workflow/routing.py`
- Add unit tests in `api/test/agents/` and workflow integration tests in `api/test/workflow/`

# RAG

- Knowledge base: markdown files in `api/app/knowledge_base/`
- Ingestion: 500-char chunks, 50-char overlap, paragraph-aware splitting
- Storage: ChromaDB (ephemeral by default, persistent if `CHROMA_PERSIST_DIRECTORY` set)
- Retrieval: similarity search with relevance scores, top_k=3
- When adding knowledge: create a `.md` file in `knowledge_base/`, restart to re-ingest

# Prompts

- All prompts centralized in `api/app/llm/prompts.py` as module-level constants
- Do not scatter prompt strings in agent classes or node functions

# Testing

- pytest with class-based test groupings mirroring source structure
- Mock agents at workflow boundaries with `MagicMock(spec=...)`
- Use `InMemoryMovieFinderAgent` for finder integration tests
- Use `make_movie()` factory for test data
- Use `TestClient(app, raise_server_exceptions=False)` for API tests
- No live Azure OpenAI or TMDB calls in default test suite
- Before creating new tests: inspect existing test files, extend existing classes when possible

# Streamlit UI

- Thin HTTP client only — all logic belongs in the API
- Chat history is client-side session state, not persisted
- Debug info rendering mirrors `DebugInfo` schema from API response

# Code Style

- Python 3.14+ syntax: `list[str]`, `str | None`, pattern matching
- Google-style docstrings on public classes and functions
- No inline code comments unless explicitly requested
- `__all__` exports in package `__init__.py` files
- Logging via `logging.getLogger(__name__)` — never print()

# File Formatting

- Preserve existing formatting and line endings
- Do not reorganize imports unless directly related to the change
